  "term": "Americans With Disabilities Act",
  "definition": "The Americans with Disabilities Act is a 1990 U.S. law that requires higher education to be accessible to people with disabilities. In this context, it is presented as a legal standard for accessibility, though the article argues that true inclusion should go beyond simply meeting its requirements.",
